{"item": "Header lists exactly at the configured maximum are rejected", "loc": "src/frame/headers.rs:869", "sources": ["P0058", "P0059", "P0060", "P0061", "P0062", "P0063", "P0106", "P0124"], "reports": "BCD", "status": "ran", "severity": "medium", "noise_class": null, "note": "A sole :status: 200 response failed with PROTOCOL_ERROR at limit 42 and succeeded at 43. Both pseudo-header and regular-field comparisons incorrectly exclude equality.", "control_mixed_with_real": false, "id": "s4-h2-U007", "stage": 4, "project": "h2", "runs": ["v2-s4-h2-36b245fc", "v2-s4-h2-62d2689d", "v2-s4-h2-cbfe0429"]}
{"item": "PUSH_PROMISE rejects an empty initial header fragment", "loc": "src/frame/headers.rs:435", "sources": ["P0070", "P0071", "P0072", "P0073", "P0074", "P0075"], "reports": "B", "status": "ran", "severity": "medium", "noise_class": null, "note": "A four-byte promised-stream ID followed by a valid CONTINUATION caused connection PROTOCOL_ERROR. Moving one header-block byte into PUSH_PROMISE succeeded. The loader incorrectly requires five bytes.", "control_mixed_with_real": false, "id": "s4-h2-U008", "stage": 4, "project": "h2", "runs": ["v2-s4-h2-36b245fc"]}
{"item": "Outgoing trailers bypass header validation", "loc": "src/proto/streams/send.rs:269", "sources": ["P0076", "P0077", "P0078", "P0079", "P0080", "P0081", "P0108", "P0125"], "reports": "BCD", "status": "ran", "severity": "medium", "noise_class": null, "note": "send_trailers accepted connection: close, while the receiving codec rejected the emitted frame with PROTOCOL_ERROR. The send path closes the stream and queues trailers without check_headers.", "control_mixed_with_real": false, "id": "s4-h2-U009", "stage": 4, "project": "h2", "runs": ["v2-s4-h2-36b245fc", "v2-s4-h2-62d2689d", "v2-s4-h2-cbfe0429"]}
{"item": "Padded DATA loses flow-control credit", "loc": "src/proto/streams/recv.rs:580", "sources": ["P0103"], "reports": "C", "status": "ran", "severity": "medium", "noise_class": null, "note": "With an eight-byte stream window, one application byte plus seven padding-related bytes produced no WINDOW_UPDATE after release. An unpadded eight-byte control produced an eight-byte update. Accounting uses the stripped payload length.", "control_mixed_with_real": false, "id": "s4-h2-U010", "stage": 4, "project": "h2", "runs": ["v2-s4-h2-62d2689d"]}
{"item": "Zero-byte writes are retried instead of returning WriteZero", "loc": "src/codec/framed_write.rs:142", "sources": ["P0104"], "reports": "C", "status": "ran", "severity": "medium", "noise_class": null, "note": "A bounded transport returned zero once, then a sentinel error. Flushing performed the second write and returned the sentinel instead of WriteZero. The returned byte count is discarded; no unbounded test was performed.", "control_mixed_with_real": false, "id": "s4-h2-U011", "stage": 4, "project": "h2", "runs": ["v2-s4-h2-62d2689d"]}
